 "about_text": "O-Town House is a small exhibition space in Los Angeles founded by curator Scott Cameron Weaver in July 2018. Occupying flexible rooms in the historic Granada Buildings on Lafayette Park, the space was built around exploring new models for presenting and producing art, encouraging dialogue between artists and the local community. Since opening, it has hosted a wide-ranging program of solo and group exhibitions, screenings, and events featuring both emerging and established artists working across painting, sculpture, film, and performance. The gallery has also extended its program abroad, participating in international fairs and collaborative presentations in Europe.",
