  "notes": "ABOUT: O-Town House is an artist-driven exhibition space founded in July 2018 by curator Scott Cameron Weaver, occupying his own apartment inside the historic Granada Buildings in the MacArthur Park neighborhood of Los Angeles. Rather than a conventional white-cube gallery, it functions as a hybrid domestic/exhibition platform, blurring living space and gallery space to encourage close, unpressured engagement with art. Its programming favors historically resonant projects—reconstructing works by overlooked Los Angeles artists like John Boskovich and hosting Suzanne Jackson, whose own Gallery 32 once operated in the same building—alongside contemporary artists such as James Benning, Cerith Wyn Evans, Adam Stamp, and Juliette Blightman. The space has also collaborated with international galleries (Lomex, Deborah Schamoni, Galería Mascota) and participated in fairs and citywide gallery events.\n\nFOUNDED: 2018\nFOUNDERS: Scott Cameron Weaver\nLOCATIONS: Los Angeles - 672 S. La Fayette Park Place, Suite 44 (Granada Buildings, MacArthur Park) (since 2018)\nROSTER: unknown (O-Town House operates as a curator-run exhibition/project space rather than a gallery with a fixed represented-artist roster; artists frequently featured include James Benning, Cerith Wyn Evans, Juliette Blightman, Adam Stamp, Suzanne Jackson, John Boskovich, Pippa Garner, Owen Fu, Gerry Bibby, Sarah Szczesny, Constantin Nitsche, Nora Schultz, Ciccio, Dean Sameshima, Tobias Spichtig, Calla Henkel & Max Pitegoff, Erlea Maneros Zabala, Bruce Yonemoto, John Knight, Kim Gordon, Michel Auder, Fabian Marti, Gina Folly, Molly Larkey, Jools Rothblatt)\nFAIRS: art berlin (2019), Condo New York (hosted at Lomex, 2019), art-o-rama Marseille (2022), Gallery Weekend Los Angeles/GPLA (2020, 2021, 2023), Basel Social Club and Liste Basel (2025–2026)\nMEMBERSHIPS: unknown (no formal association or curated-list membership found; participates in the Gallery Weekend Los Angeles citywide platform)\nSOURCES: ht